  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;is a complex number, such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. In which of the following cases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies in the&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ι</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ι</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> quadrant? <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
